# The Chrome the references are captured from: the release naive's library is built of (the owner's rule: the
# target is the Chrome of the library's Chromium, 158 today), not whatever the runner's image carries.
# fingerprint.yml refuses a major that is not the library's.
#
# One Chromium for the project (the owner, 2026-11-17): the library is 158.0.8127.36, and so is the reference, as
# near as a package exists. On Linux no channel serves 158 on that day: stable is 157.0.8103.78, beta has moved on
# to 159, and 158.0.8127.36 is out for Windows, macOS and Android only. So the reference is the last Linux package
# of the branch, 158.0.8127.18 of the beta, by its hash: the same branch 8127 as the library, which fingerprint.yml
# checks. When 158 is stable on Linux the workflow takes it by itself (the current stable is tried first), and
# CHROME_REFERENCE_DEB can go empty. At the library's next Chromium the major here moves with it.
CHROME_REFERENCE_MAJOR=158
CHROME_REFERENCE_DEB="https://dl.google.com/linux/chrome/deb/pool/main/g/google-chrome-beta/google-chrome-beta_158.0.8127.18-1_amd64.deb"
CHROME_REFERENCE_DEB_SHA256="461c4af29c34d038d1b28c6dc2951e5cdb183776f2d644510543ea108a345e68"
